er.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.8b6ee04bda65b96e2475b9411e65a04d86e359f7.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Warning","headline":"Flood Warning issued October 23 at 2:25PM MDT until October 23 at 5:00PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"* WHAT...The Flood Warning is cancelled for a portion of south\ncentral Colorado, including the following areas, Mineral and Rio\nGrande.\n\nThe heavy rain has ended. Please continue to heed remaining road\nclosures.\n\nA Flood Watch remains in effect until 600 PM MDT Friday for a portion\nof south central Colorado...\n\n* WHERE...Southwestern Saguache, Central Mineral and Western Rio\nGrande Counties...\n\n* WHEN...Until 500 PM MDT.\n\n* IMPACTS...Several structures are flooded and evacuations have\noccurred from Wolf Creek Ranch to Fun Valley. Some roads remain\nclosed due to flooding including highway 160 and FR380. The Park\nCreek bridge has been washed away with considerable debris in the\nwater.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 223 PM MDT, Stream gauges indicate flooding continues for the\nSouth Fork Rio Grande, Rio Grande between South Fork and Del\nNorte, and other area streams.\n- The South Fork Rio Grande and other area streams are past their\ncrests and are continuing to fall. The South Fork Rio Grande is\nexpected to fall back below Flood Stage late Friday night.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nDel Norte, South Fork, Wagon Wheel Gap and Creede.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-23T17:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Mineral, CO; Rio Grande, CO; Saguache, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.e3049d31a745a79dc4d8679995e0c0fe5a83679c.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.e3049d31a745a79dc4d8679995e0c0fe5a83679c.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-10-23T19:17:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KPUB 231917 AFDPUB Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Pueblo CO 117 PM MDT Fri Oct 23 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Heavy rain threat wi